Activity # 5: Installing Relevant Technologies for Cyber Threat Monitoring

Objective:
Set up essential cybersecurity tools and practice secure installation, verification, and Git-based workflow using Git and GitHub.

Part 1: Download Required Tools

Download the following:

    Gpg4win
            https://gpg4win.org/download.html

    Git
            https://git-scm.com/

    GitHub Desktop (Optional)
           https://desktop.github.com/download/

    GitHub CLI
           https://cli.github.com/

Part 2: Install Gpg4win & Verify Installer (IMPORTANT)
[Step 1]
    Install Gpg4win
    Open the downloaded installer
    Click Next → Install → Finish
[Step 2]
    Verify Installer Using PowerShell
    Open PowerShell
    Navigate to your Downloads folder:
           cd $env:USERPROFILE\Downloads
    Run this command to generate file hash:

          Get-FileHash .\gpg4win-*.exe

    Go back to the official Gpg4win website
    Compare the hash value:
    If it matches → File is safe
    If not → Do NOT install


Part 3: Install Other Tools
    Install Git
    Open the Git installer
    Click Next until installation starts
    Keep default settings (recommended)
    Click Install → Finish


Install GitHub CLI
    Open the installer
    Click Next → Install → Finish
    Open Command Prompt / PowerShell
    Verify installation:

            gh --version

Install GitHub Desktop (Optional)
    Open installer
    Sign in using your GitHub account
    Follow setup instructions

