Part 5: Git Configuration

    Open Git Bash inside your folder, then run:

            git config --global user.name "Your Cybersecurity Handle"
            git config --global user.email "your@email.com"
            git config --list

Part 6: Authenticate Using GitHub CLI
Step-by-Step:

    Open terminal (Git Bash or PowerShell)
    Run:

           gh auth login

    Follow the prompts:
    Choose: GitHub.com
    Choose: HTTPS
    Choose: Login with a web browser
    A code will appear → copy it
    Browser will open:
    Paste the code
    Click Authorize
    Once successful, you will see:

            Authentication complete.

Part 7: Upload Your Project to GitHub

1. Initialize Repository

    Right-click folder → Open Git Bash here

           git init
           git add .
           git commit -m "Initial cyber attack log upload"

2. Create Repository Online

    Go to GitHub
    Click New Repository
    Repository name = your folder name
    DO NOT check “Add README”
    Click Create Repository
    Connect & Push

           git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/nameofproject.git
           git branch -M main
           git push -u origin main

3. Add Tag
           git tag v1.0
           git push origin v1.0

